 "title": "Interview Question: Never Use AI for This Task",
 "topic": "ai tools",
 "summary": "The creator discusses how to answer the interview question about which task you would never use AI for. The lesson is to distinguish between understanding information (where AI helps) and synthesizing or applying it (where human judgment must take over).",
 "key_points": [
  "Recognize that the interview question is testing how dependent you are on AI for your work.",
  "Distinguish between understanding your work and synthesizing your work.",
  "The internet made information free, and AI made understanding free.",
  "The one task to never depend on AI for is synthesizing that information, drawing insights, and applying it.",
  "AI's job ends at understanding, and your job begins at synthesizing."
 ],
 "content": "INTERVIEW QUESTION WHAT IS THE 1 TASK FOR WHICH YOU WILL NEVER USE AI? If the interviewer asks you what is that one task for which you will never use AI, the interviewer is not asking your question, he or she is checking how dependent you are on AI for your work. So you need to distinguish between understanding your work and synthesizing your work. Now before I tell you how to do that, I'm Satish Torani. I help you become an articulate speaker, so you can speak to the point. Here's what you can say. The internet made information free for everyone. AI has made understanding free for everyone. But the one task for which I will never depend on AI is synthesizing that information, which means that once I've got the information, I've understood the information, the insights that I will draw and the application of that information which I will decide is going to be up to me. So AI's job will end at understanding. My job will begin at synthesizing. SPEAK TO THE POINT. DM FOR A FREE CONSULT. Instagram reel/post by Satish Torani l Speak to the Point. Text / caption: Interview question - what is the one task for which you will never use AI?",
